# HK Form 1-3 Chemistry Curriculum vs PhET Coverage Analysis

> This document maps every chemistry topic in the Hong Kong Junior Secondary Integrated Science curriculum (Forms 1–3) to available PhET simulations, identifies gaps, and proposes alternatives.

## Context
- **Grant**: HK Government "AI for Empowering Learning and Teaching" — HK$500,000 (~US$64,200) per school
- **Requirement**: AI-assisted teaching in at least 3 subjects by the school
- **Platform**: PhET Interactive Simulations (free, HTML5, multilingual)

---

## Coverage Matrix

### Form 1 — Foundational Chemistry

| # | Curriculum Topic | PhET Simulation | Status |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | **States of Matter** (solid, liquid, gas properties) | ✅ [States of Matter](https://phet.colorado.edu/en/simulations/states-of-matter) | **Covered** |
| 2 | **Particle Theory** (matter is made of particles) | ✅ [States of Matter: Basics](https://phet.colorado.edu/en/simulations/states-of-matter-basics) | **Covered** |
| 3 | **Changes of Physical State** (melting, boiling, evaporation) | ✅ States of Matter (heating/cooling controls) | **Covered** |
| 4 | **Dissolving** (solvent, solute, solution, rate of dissolving) | ✅ [Sugar and Salt Solutions](https://phet.colorado.edu/en/simulations/sugar-and-salt-solutions) / [Concentration](https://phet.colorado.edu/en/simulations/concentration) | **Covered** |
| 5 | **Solubility** | ✅ [Molarity](https://phet.colorado.edu/en/simulations/molarity) / Concentration | **Covered** |
| 6 | **Filtration** | ⚠️ No dedicated PhET sim | **GAP** |
| 7 | **Evaporation as separation** | ⚠️ Partially via Concentration sim (evaporation slider) | **Partial** |
| 8 | **Elements, Compounds, Mixtures** (classification) | ✅ [Build a Molecule](https://phet.colorado.edu/en/simulations/build-a-molecule) | **Covered** |
| 9 | **Metals vs Non-metals** (physical properties) | ❌ No PhET sim | **GAP** |
| 10 | **Molecular Models / Chemical Formulae** | ✅ Build a Molecule / [Molecule Shapes](https://phet.colorado.edu/en/simulations/molecule-shapes) | **Covered** |

