## Summary Scorecard

| Category | Covered | Partial | Gap | Total |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **Form 1** | 7 | 2 | 1 | 10 |
| **Form 2** | 4 | 2 | 3 | 9 |
| **Form 3** | 8 | 2 | 3 | 13 |
| **Overall** | **19** | **6** | **7** | **32** |

> **PhET covers ~59% fully, ~19% partially, and has gaps in ~22% of the HK curriculum.**

---

## ⚠️ Critical Gaps (No PhET Simulation Available)

These 7 topics have **no PhET simulation** and will need alternatives:

| Topic | Form | Why it Matters | Recommended Alternative |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Filtration** | F1 | Core separation technique in HK syllabus | [ChemCollective](https://chemcollective.org/) or custom AI-guided sim |
| **Metals vs Non-metals** | F1 | Required classification topic | Custom interactive (AI-powered comparison tool) |
| **Gas Tests** (O₂, CO₂, H₂) | F2 | Key practical skills in HK exams | [Amrita Virtual Lab](https://vlab.amrita.edu/) or custom sim |
| **Combustion** | F2 | Linked to respiration & energy topics | [ChemCollective](https://chemcollective.org/) or video + AI Q&A |
| **Respiration as Chemical Reaction** | F2 | Biology-chemistry crossover | LabXchange or custom AI explanation |
| **Rocks, Minerals & Metal Extraction** | F3 | Earth science crossover topic | [Virtual Labs India](https://vlab.co.in/) or custom sim |
| **Oxidation & Reduction** | F3 | Foundation for senior chemistry | [ChemCollective](https://chemcollective.org/) redox virtual labs |
| **Distillation / Crystallization** | F3 | Separation technique required | [Amrita Virtual Lab](https://vlab.amrita.edu/) fractional distillation sim |

---

## ✅ Recommended Strategy

### Option A: PhET + Supplementary Platforms (Faster, Lower Cost)
1. Use **PhET** for the 19 fully-covered + 6 partially-covered topics (78%)
2. Integrate **ChemCollective** for gap topics related to chemical reactions (combustion, redox)
3. Integrate **Amrita Virtual Lab** for separation techniques (distillation, crystallization, gas tests)
4. Use **AI (Gemini)** to bridge partial gaps with interactive Q&A and guided explanations

### Option B: PhET + Custom AI Simulations (More Grant-Aligned, Higher Impact)
1. Use **PhET** for covered topics
2. Build **custom AI-powered interactive simulations** for the 7 gap topics using Gemini
3. This approach is **more impressive for the grant** as it demonstrates AI integration directly
4. Can be developed incrementally and showcases the school's innovation

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Option B is recommended** — it maximizes the AI component (which the grant specifically funds), fills all curriculum gaps, and positions the project as a truly innovative solution. The custom sims don't need to be as polished as PhET; they just need to be functional and AI-enhanced.

---

## 6 Partially-Covered Topics — How AI Can Fill the Gaps

| Topic | Current PhET Limitation | AI Enhancement |
|---|---|---|
| Evaporation as separation | Only a slider in Concentration sim | AI explains the separation process step-by-step |
| Composition of Air | Molecules and Light shows molecules, not composition | AI chatbot provides composition data & quiz |
| Preparation of Salts | Acid-Base sim doesn't show salt formation explicitly | AI walks through salt preparation procedures |
| Ionic Bonding | Atomic Interactions shows forces, not ionic transfer | AI animates electron transfer with explanations |
| Covalent Bonding | Molecule Polarity shows polarity, not bond formation | AI explains shared electron pairs interactively |
| Neutralization Products | Acid-Base sim shows neutralization but not products | AI identifies products and writes equations |
